Let us write $\vec x \permprefeq \vec y$ if $\vec x$ is a permutation of prefixes of $\vec y$, i.e.\ $\vec x = x_0, \dots, x_{n-1}$ and $\vec y = y_0 , \dots , y_{n-1}$ and there is a permutation $\pi : [n] \to [n]$ s.t.\ each $x_i$ is a prefix of $y_{\pi i}$.
